VCPE Contribute-Back License, version 1.0

Copyright (c) 2026 surelynotvain

"VCPE" means Vain's C Portable Engine: every file in this repository (engine source, runtime, tools, docs and
assets), in any version from 3.0 on, and any work based on those files. "Your project" means a game, demake,
program or other work that uses VCPE. "Engine changes" means any change to VCPE files, and any new file that
is part of the engine rather than of your project (a new engine module, tool or fix), in source form.

1. Permission. You may use, copy, build, run and distribute VCPE, alone or as part of your project, free of
   charge, under the conditions below.

2. Contribute your engine changes back. If you distribute your project, or VCPE itself, with engine changes,
   you must submit those engine changes as a pull request to https://github.com/surelynotvain/vcpe (or the
   location the copyright holder names there). Submit them no later than the first public distribution that
   contains them. You grant the copyright holder a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free license to use, modify
   and relicense what you submit. Whether a pull request is merged is up to the copyright holder; once it is
   submitted, you have met this condition.

3. Your own code stays yours. Your project's own code, art, data and other content are not engine changes.
   This license does not require you to publish them or send them to anyone.

4. Credit. Your project's credits, readme or about screen must state that it uses Vain's C Portable Engine
   (VCPE) by surelynotvain.

5. Notice. Copies of VCPE source must keep this license and the copyright notice above.

6. Third-party material. Material in VCPE that comes from third parties remains under its owners' terms and
   is not licensed by this license: the pictures in engineassets/ and the image data generated from them
   (src/vcpe_errimg.h, src/vcpe_loadimg.h), and libraries VCPE uses from the pspdev toolchain (such as
   stb_truetype). Replace those pictures with your own if their terms do not allow your use.

7. Termination. If you break these conditions, your permission ends. It is restored if you fix the breach
   within 30 days of being notified.

8. No warranty. VCPE is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including the
   warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. In no event shall the
   authors or copyright holders be liable for any claim, damages or other liability, whether in an action of
   contract, tort or otherwise, arising from, out of or in connection with VCPE or the use of or other dealings
   in VCPE.

VCPE 1.0 and 2.0 were released under the MIT license, and the copies of them already released keep that
license. This license applies to VCPE 3.0 and every later version.
